er</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Hassell</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Inhibition of limb chondrogenesis in vitro by vitamin A</article-title><source>Dev Biol</source><year>1978</year><volume>64</volume><fpage>31</fpage><lpage>47</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">566229</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Solursh</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Meier</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The selective inhibition of mucopolysaccharide synthesis by vitamin A treatment of cultured chick embryo chondrocytes</article-title><source>Calcif Tissue Res</source><year>1973</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>131</fpage><lpage>142</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4271531</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zimmerman</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Tsambos</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Evaluation of the sensitive step of inhibition of chondrogenesis by retinoids in limb mesenchymal cells in vitro</article-title><source>Cell Differentiation</source><year>1985</year><volume>17</volume><fpage>95</fpage><lpage>103</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4042164</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Benya</surname><given-names>PD</given-names></name><name><surname>Padilla</surname><given-names>SR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Modulation of the rabbit chondrocyte phenotype by retinoic acid terminates type II collagen synthesis without inducing type I collagen: the modulated phenotype differs from that produced by subculture</article-title><source>Dev Biol</source><year>1986</year><volume>118</volu